    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0522" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg412"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5612A/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tobin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-29T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                                1928—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>11. The Department handed the Chargé d’Affaires of the Netherlands Legation,
                    today, a draft of a proposed treaty of arbitration between the United States and
                    the Netherlands.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d335-f1"/> The provisions of the draft
                    operate to extend the policy of arbitration enunciated in the Convention signed
                    at Washington, May 2, 1908,<anchor n="30" xml:id="d335-f2"/> which expires on
                    March 25, 1929. The language of the draft is identical in effect with that of
                    the Arbitration Treaty recently signed with France<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d335-f3"/> and with the draft arbitration treaties already submitted
                    to other governments in the general program for the extension of these
                    principles. The text of the proposed treaty will be forwarded in the next
                    pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olds</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
